fused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {"implementer": 1}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 2, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "The dashboard now shows a \"Watcher stopped\" state when `/api/live` reports `watcher_stopped`, and tells the user to restart the tracker instead of turning watching on. I read the diff and reran the three spec checks myself. `pnpm --dir web test` and `tsc -b` pass, and `pnpm --dir web lint` ran clean. I only saw the tail of the test output, so I didn't count the tests. I didn't run the app, so I haven't seen the pill or the callouts in a browser.\n\nThe implementer changed only the four files the spec names, and I left `web/src/lib/home.test.ts` alone:\n- **`lib/home.ts`:** adds `WATCHER_STOPPED_SENTENCE`, `watcherCallout` and `liveState`.\n- **`LiveStatus.tsx`:** adds the \"Watcher stopped\" pill state with a warn-coloured dot. The panel shows the stopped sentence in that state.\n- **`CurrentMatchView.tsx`:** the no-match branch uses `watcherCallout`. The opening-hand, intermission and in-match branches show the stopped callout first.\n- **`FirstRun.tsx`:** the first step's detail now reads `watcherCallout(live) ?? NOT_WATCHING_SENTENCE`.\n\nI didn't run `pnpm build` or the Python checks, since the spec doesn't list them and nothing in Python changed.", "ttft_ms": 1268, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 12276, "uuid": "a9ca866b-46ab-4c56-a280-569ab0a8b47b", "ttft_stream_ms": 868, "time_to_request_ms": 16, "first_content_frame_ms": 868, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 1}
